To implement bubble sort for the given input, you can follow these steps:

1. Define a function `bubbleSort(int arr[], int n)` to perform bubble sort on the array passed as argument.
2. Iterate through all the elements from the first to the second last element (n-1).
3. Compare adjacent elements and swap them if they are in the wrong order.
4. Repeat step 3 until no swaps are made in one iteration, which indicates that the list is sorted.

Here's the implementation in C++:

```c++
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    bool swapped = true;
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1 && swapped; i++) {
        swapped = false;
        for (int j = 0; j < n - I - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                swap(arr[j], arr[j+1]);
                swapped = true;
            }
        }
    }
}

